** The NED test case, held whole in every process: the executePythonCode generator below changes
** nothing, but code run on the model while the mesh is described is a reason for the replicated-elements
** fallback (domaindecomposition.distributedelements.reasonsToReplicateElements). Contact and ties run
** distributed, so this keeps the fallback under test (testfiles/mpi/check_element_distribution.py).
*material, name=VonMises, id=myMaterial, provider=edelweiss
210000, 0.3, 550, 1000, 200, 1400, 1

*section, name=section1, material=myMaterial, type=plane, thickness=1
all

*job, name=c3d8job, domain=2d
*solver, solver=NEDMPI, name=theSolver
output-frequency=1
*modelGenerator, generator=planeRectQuad, name=gen
l=10
h=10
nX=2
nY=2
elType=CPE4
elProvider=edelweiss

*modelGenerator, generator=executePythonCode, name=nothing
pass

*output, type=computetimemonitor

*step, type=adaptiveForExplicitSimulations, solver=theSolver
maxInc=1e0, minInc=1e-2, maxNumInc=10000, maxIter=25, stepLength=1
>>dirichlet, name=left, nSet=gen_left, field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0
>>dirichlet, name=bottom, nSet=gen_leftBottom, field=displacement, 2=0
>>dirichlet, name=right, nSet=gen_right, field=displacement, 2=0.2
